p('The CSP comparator was near binary chance on both cohorts and strongly favored left-hand labels. On Cho2017, shared input reduced mean left-hand recall from 46.79% to 37.52%, while right-hand recall increased from 72.86% to 79.10%. On Lee2019, the corresponding recalls changed from 75.56% to 72.69% and from 55.46% to 58.75%. These asymmetric changes are retained rather than hidden by balanced accuracy. They were calculated from the frozen outputs as descriptive checks and did not trigger any threshold, label, adapter, or model change.'),
